# Compiled Executables
*.exe
*.out
/main
# NO EXCEPTIONS HERE. `skald-ui/skald_codegen.exe` — the generator the app
# spawns for both preview and Generate — used to be un-ignored and tracked. It
# drifted nine backend commits behind its own source, so in a fresh clone every
# exposed-parameter knob was a silent no-op during preview, the voice-steal
# anti-click fix was un-shipped, and CI's green badge certified a compiler no
# user ran (BUGS.md SKB-001, roadmap packet A2, §3.1).
#
# It is built from source now, on the two commands a contributor types:
# `npm start` and `npm run make` run skald-ui/scripts/ensure-codegen.mjs, which
# calls skald-backend/build_codegen.bat (SKALD_ODIN -> vendored .tools -> PATH).
# The app then checks `skald_codegen.exe -version` against the backend sources
# and refuses to spawn a mismatched binary with a visible banner
# (skald-ui/src/main/codegenStamp.ts), and CI rebuilds it and gates the
# generated files against it.
#
# The ordering constraint that used to block this is satisfied: Odin toolchain
# resolution landed in 53b807c (packet A13), so a checkout with no binary and no
# compiler now fails loudly and actionably at launch instead of not starting at
# all (roadmap §4.8). Re-adding a tracked binary would re-open SKB-001 — the
# packaging path already builds it, and `prestart` deliberately does not abort
# the app when the build fails.

# Agent/assistant working directories
.claude/
fable-prompts/

# Test output
skald-backend/tests/out/

# Build artifacts
*.o
*.obj
*.dll
*.so
*.pdb

# Compiled manual. `scripts/manual/build-manual.mjs` rebuilds skald-manual.html
# (~2 MB) and skald-manual.pdf (~10 MB) from docs/manual-source/, so the build
# output stays out of git for the same reason the codegen binary should: a
# committed artifact drifts from its source silently. Packaging is responsible
# for building it (roadmap packet B6).
/docs/manual/

# The acceptance harness's codegen target. run_acceptance.bat copies
# _stub.odin.template over this before the self-test and then overwrites it once
# per fixture, so a tracked copy is guaranteed-stale build output that dirties
# the tree on every run — the same class as the tracked codegen binary above.
# The template is the source; this is its output.
/skald-backend/acceptance/generated_audio/generated_audio.odin

# regen_generated.bat's scratch dir: fresh emission for the checked-in
# generated_audio.odin copies, compared against the committed files and thrown
# away. Same role as tests/golden/.gen/.
/skald-backend/.regen/

# Skald-generated scratch output
/skald-ui/generated_audio.odin
/skald-backend/generated_audio.odin
/skald-backend/gen_soft/
/skald-backend/tests/golden/.gen/

